  "question": {
    "text": "A tangent drawn to hyperbola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math> forms a triangle of area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> square units, with coordinate axes. If the eccentricity of hyperbola is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
